1
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:12,387
[grunts]

2
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,931
Hold all my calls.

3
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:17,726
[giggling]

4
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:19,394
♪ Boss Baby ♪

5
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:23,523
♪ I'm the boss, Boss Baby
Boss boss, Boss Baby, boss boss ♪

6
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:28,653
♪ Watch a itty bitty kid get large
I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪

7
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:31,114
♪ Stroller rolling
Up and down the boulevard ♪

8
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:33,742
♪ I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪

9
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:39,581
♪ I run this house, I rule this crib
Change my diaper, son, where's my bib? ♪

10
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:42,417
♪ Don't pacify, you just got to pay me ♪

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,961
-♪ Who's in charge? ♪
-♪ Me, the Boss Baby ♪

12
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:50,967
[doorbell rings]

13
00:00:52,969 --> 00:00:57,223
"Good morning, sir or ma'am.
I am a Lowly Apprentice Do-Good Trooper,

14
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:59,934
looking to advance
to Lofty Squire Do-Good Trooper.

15
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,687
To accomplish this dream,
I need just one more sticker

16
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:05,732
for my achievement helmet,
the Neighborhood Service sticker.

17
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:09,194
It requires me to help out
every single neighbor on my block.

18
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:13,031
The question is,
how can I do good for you today?"

19
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:15,867
Uh, you wanna sweep my porch?

20
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:19,621
Ooh!

21
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:22,248
[Tim whistling]

22
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:24,876
[continues whistling]

23
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:27,504
[doorbell rings]

24
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:30,548
"Good morning, sir or ma'am."

25
00:01:30,632 --> 00:01:32,634
Clearly, "ma'am."

26
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:34,677
Do-Good Troopers never pre-judge.

27
00:01:52,445 --> 00:01:54,989
Yes! One last neighbor to...

28
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:07,335
Well, I am out of the Do-Good Troopers!

29
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:10,213
-Whoa, buddy. Everything okay?
-What happened?

30
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:14,259
Nothing. I'm just never gonna be
a Lofty Squire Do-Good Trooper ever!

31
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:17,637
-So, what's the point?
-[Dad] Timbo, want to talk about it?

32
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:20,390
[tapping on glass]

33
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:30,358
Guys, I'm in the middle of breakfast here.

34
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:32,068
[cat shrieking]

35
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:34,737
Is that a box of cat?

36
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,531
Oh, yes, it is, sir.

37
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:40,368
Jimbo and I were doing our morning patrol
of the neighborhood when...

38
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:42,412
-I saw a fire truck!
-[cat growling]

39
00:02:42,495 --> 00:02:45,707
And also, we got jumped
by one of Bootsy's kittens. Oh!

40
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,167
They're getting bolder.

41
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:51,504
-They're getting vicious!
-[screams] Not the face! Not the face!

42
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,298
-[cat shrieking]
-[Staci grunting]

43
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:55,008
-[punches landing]
-[Jimbo yells]

44
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:59,637
Miss McCrackin's house? Tim, honey,
there's nothing there to be afraid of.

45
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:02,557
But it's old and dark
and creepy and gross.

46
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,809
I can feel my breakfast coming up
just thinking about--

47
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:05,977
-[Mom] Bucket.
-[Dad] Clear!

48
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,938
-I'm not actually throwing up.
-Oh, good.

49
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:10,565
Honey, Wendi's a nice lady.

50
00:03:10,648 --> 00:03:14,193
She goes to Book Club,
she knits me a sweater every Christmas.

51
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,738
She-- I don't know.
She probably pays her taxes.

52
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:19,866
-Danny Petrosky told me--
-Ugh, that kid.

53
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:23,953
Danny said Miss McCrackin
turns kids into robots.

54
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,204
[snorts, laughs]

55
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:28,499
Robots? Oh, man,
that Danny sure cracks me up.

56
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:33,046
Tim, no one is able to turn a kid
into a robot. I know you know that.

57
00:03:33,129 --> 00:03:35,506
Do you really want me to take that chance?

58
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,967
No chance, sport. We promise.

59
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,345
-[Tim] Um...
-[cat yowls]

60
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:43,973
Did I ever tell you that when I was
your age, I wasn't even allowed

61
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,392
-to be a Do-Good Trooper?
-Because you were a girl?

62
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:49,646
No. It was because
they thought I had a big head,

63
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:53,441
and it wouldn't fit into the helmet,
which is obviously not the case.

64
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:55,860
Girls' heads just grow faster than boys'.

65
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:58,029
-That's science.
-That's not science.

66
00:03:58,112 --> 00:04:01,199
-Uh, agree to disagree.
-I don't agree to that.

67
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,036
The point is,
your mother's head is lovely.

68
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:09,666
Thank you, Ted. But the other point is,
you can't judge a book by its cover.

69
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:13,503
The Troopers judged me, and now
that's what you're doing with Wendi,

70
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:14,837
and it's wrong.

71
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:17,632
Timothy Leslie Templeton.

72
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:20,718
Are you listening to me?
What are you even looking at out--?

73
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:24,472
 -I have problems! Focus on me!
-[cat meowing]

74
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:26,641
-[cat hisses, growling]
-[Staci chuckling]

75
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:28,601
[shrieking]

76
00:04:29,394 --> 00:04:30,770
-Got it! Again!
-[snarling]

77
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:35,024
-Okay, now, what do we do with the kitty?
-Let's mail it to the ocean.

78
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:36,943
Not how the postal system works. Staci.

79
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:40,280
We could take it to the junkyard
and see if they'll strip it for parts.

80
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:43,074
-Tempting, but no.
-[Tim] I don't wanna be a robot!

81
00:04:43,157 --> 00:04:47,704
Timothy Templeton,
we are going to help Wendi.

82
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:51,082
You can't bail on neighborhood service
just because a nice lady chooses to live

83
00:04:51,165 --> 00:04:53,084
 in a weird old house
with a bunch of cats.

84
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:55,378
[gasps] House full of cats?

85
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:58,798
We are going to march over there
and do our Do-Good duty!

86
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:02,260
"Our"? Sounds like you're really
holding onto something, Janice.

87
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:03,344
[slurps]

88
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,597
Listen to your mother, Tim!

89
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:10,018
I have an outside-the-box idea.
Let's roll.

90
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:11,311
-Yeah!
-[Jimbo chuckles]

91
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:15,023
Suit up, Trooper.
Let me put the baby down,

92
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:17,859
and then we are going earn you
that helmet sticker.

93
00:05:18,276 --> 00:05:20,903
Oh, I guess your dad got him.

94
00:05:24,407 --> 00:05:29,329
[cats yowling]

95
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:31,164
Why so many cats?

96
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:35,668
Who cares? It's the perfect cat prison.

97
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:41,924
Shove this killer kitty in there,
and Wendi, as unhinged as she is,

98
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:44,302
will be thrilled to gain another fleabag.

99
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:47,972
You know, because she's... [meows]
Now, hit it, Big J!

100
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,769
[screaming]

101
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:56,773
[cats yowling, echoing]

102
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:03,321
[meowing continues]

103
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:08,242
[cat meowing]

104
00:06:11,746 --> 00:06:14,165
-I wish you nothing but the best.
-[shrieking]

105
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:16,501
[screams, pants]

106
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,919
That was surprisingly easy.

107
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:19,796
[grunts, screams]

108
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:20,755
[both gasp]

109
00:06:20,838 --> 00:06:22,340
-[Mom] Come on, Tim.
-[gasps]

110
00:06:24,884 --> 00:06:29,597
-What do we do, sir? What do we do?
-Mom and Tim. Cats.

111
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:32,767
But Mom and Tim! But cats.

112
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,562
Come on, what's it gonna be, Boss?

113
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:39,440
Staci, I guess we've got to go...

114
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:43,277
into the belly of the den
of the house of the nest of cats!

115
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:46,739
Huh?

116
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:51,160
Don't hate me for being prepared.

117
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:54,997
Cats are evil but dumb.
If we act just like them,

118
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:58,626
we can go in there,
stay off their radar, and save Jimbo!

119
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,753
[sighs] My shame is complete.

120
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:08,594
[Boss] It's pitch black in here.
Can cats see in the dark?

121
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,723
[Staci] Uh, I think that's dogs. Cats are
the ones that can smell your fear.

122
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:14,183
[Boss] No, that's dogs.

123
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,686
[Staci] Um, sir, I'm happy
to sit here in the dark,

124
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:19,647
arguing about which animals
have which lame superpower,

125
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,983
but if we're gonna find Jimbo...

126
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:23,693
[cats meowing]

127
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:25,361
[hissing]

128
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:32,452
Oh, aren't you little fur babies
the cutest?

129
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:37,957
I bet you two strays are dying
for a dish of milk.

130
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:41,210
[cats yowling, hissing]

131
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,550
-[whispers] Where's Jimbo?
-Back there?

132
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:50,303
[doorbell rings]

133
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,847
Ugh! It's probably people.

134
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:57,185
Now's our chance.
Let's go check that back room for Jim--

135
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:03,608
I don't know if I can do this. Ahh!
Scratch that. I can, but I don't want to.

136
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:07,195
Just pull yourself together
and don't make any sudden movements.

137
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:09,280
Sudden movements?
But you just slapped me--

138
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:11,157
Forget about it. Just blend in.

139
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:13,784
Meow?

140
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:20,833
Good morning, sir or... ma'am.
Ma'am. So, um, never mind. Bye!

141
00:08:20,917 --> 00:08:23,961
Wendi, always a pleasure.
Here's the lowdown.

142
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:26,631
My son needs to help you
with something around the house

143
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:29,342
to earn his last
Do-Good Trooper helmet sticker.

144
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:33,721
It's very important to me.
But to him as well.

145
00:08:33,804 --> 00:08:35,890
I'm busy, Janice. I've got cats.

146
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:40,645
And I respect that, but you know kids,
how they just won't let go of that thing

147
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:44,065
they want more than anything,
which is my Timmy here.

148
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:45,733
Ugh!

149
00:08:45,816 --> 00:08:48,152
The sooner we start, the sooner we leave.

150
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:52,907
Fine. Got a lot of stuff in the backyard
I've been meaning to haul away.

151
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:58,079
Would that be good enough for you?
I mean, for your son Tim?

152
00:08:58,162 --> 00:09:00,998
Uh, the "outside-ier," the better.

153
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:06,254
Have at it.

154
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:11,717
[robot beeping, whirring]

155
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:17,515
I used to be a little boy like you.

156
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:20,726
[screams]

157
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:26,190
-[screams]
-Well, this was unexpected,

158
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:29,902
but can't wait
to get "McCrackin" on this, Wendi!

159
00:09:29,986 --> 00:09:33,197
House is off-limits.
That's non-negotiable.

160
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:37,868
Ring the bell when you're done.
Or you could just leave. [chuckles]

161
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:40,997
-Do that one.
-You've got yourself a deal!

162
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:44,542
Ugh! My fur babies don't like
smelling other people.

163
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:52,425
This'll be fun! Just think of it as one
of your Dekker Moonboots adventures.

164
00:09:52,508 --> 00:09:57,179
Don't you get it, Mom? This is the metal
she uses to turn kids into robots!

165
00:09:57,263 --> 00:10:01,017
This evil is everything
Dekker Moonboots stands against!

166
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,728
Tim, if you're trying
to get out of doing some work,

167
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,730
 the scope of which I did not anticipate--

168
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:09,108
I'm not, I swear!
I just love my body the way it is.

169
00:10:09,191 --> 00:10:13,237
And that's a beautiful thing, Tim,
but it's not an excuse.

170
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:15,197
Grab some metal.
You're building character.

171
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:16,949
[sighs]

172
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:21,162
[cats meowing]

173
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,873
I'm getting the sense
they don't believe we're cats.

174
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:26,751
This is the only way
we're gonna find and rescue Jimbo.

175
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:30,546
We gotta make them believe. [grunting]

176
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:35,259
[shrieking]

177
00:10:35,343 --> 00:10:38,971
Somebody has
a lot of repressed hostility. Fine!

178
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:43,893
[meowing]

179
00:10:43,976 --> 00:10:45,061
[chuckles]

180
00:10:48,064 --> 00:10:48,898
[groans]

181
00:10:48,981 --> 00:10:52,610
-[meowing]
-[heaves, coughs]

182
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:55,196
[continues coughing]

183
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,739
Oh! Oh, that came out.

184
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,578
Mondays. Am I right?

185
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,665
It's all for Jimbo. It's all for Jimbo!

186
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,919
[giggling]

187
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:13,255
-Think they bought it?
-After what you did to that litter box?

188
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:16,425
-[mimics explosion]
-I don't know what you think you saw,

189
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:20,179
 but I went in there strictly for show.
[chuckles] Nothing happened.

190
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:21,764
-[growling]
-[Boss] We've been made!

191
00:11:21,847 --> 00:11:26,811
-I pooped in a box for nothing.
-[cat growling]

192
00:11:26,894 --> 00:11:29,021
[sniffing]

193
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:31,107
[snarling]

194
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,610
We did it! We're in!

195
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:38,572
Let's go get Jimbo! And never speak
of that litter incident again.

196
00:11:41,826 --> 00:11:45,037
Too big. Safe from being robotomized.

197
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:48,207
[grunts] Tim, that doesn't go on your arm.

198
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:49,917
And it never will!

199
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:52,336
Come on, back to work.

200
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,342
[gasps, whimpers]

201
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:00,678
[metal clinking]

202
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:10,521
[cats meowing, hissing]

203
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:16,026
[metal clinking]

204
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:19,488
-Um...
-[metal clinking]

205
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,907
Some sort of musical performance?

206
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:27,246
[gasps] Wait, look!

207
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:33,502
-Jimbo!
-Sorry, we have to cat fight now.

208
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:36,172
-Did he say "cat fight"? [grunts]
-[Jimbo yells]

209
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:39,008
[grunts]

210
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:46,682
[grunting] Tim, I'm going to give myself
a hernia working for this sticker.

211
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:48,934
Help me move... whatever this is.

212
00:12:49,018 --> 00:12:51,020
I think you mean "whoever."

213
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:55,775
I think you mean "whomever," and I think
you're not learning your lesson.

214
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:01,030
Timmy, I know you have
a powerful imagination,

215
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:03,532
but I need you to remember
why we're doing this.

216
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,826
Because judging a book
by its cover is wrong,

217
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:09,079
because Mommy's head
was and is of regulation size,

218
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:11,999
and because you're the best, sweetest,
most helpful little boy,

219
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:13,626
and you deserve that sticker!

220
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:16,128
So, what do you say? Should we go earn it?

221
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:20,966
Hey, Timmy! Miss McCrackin is a nice...

222
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,885
-[metal slicing]
-[Timmy grunting]

223
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:24,845
-[grunts]
-[both gasp]

224
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:27,056
[metal slicing]

225
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:33,312
[whispers] I bet she's always wanted
a grown-up robot.

226
00:13:33,395 --> 00:13:37,274
[whimpers] Everything's normal,
normal, normal, normal.

227
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:40,236
-[snarls]
-[grunts]

228
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:44,114
-Jimbo, why are you doing this?
-It's the only way to stay alive in here.

229
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:45,741
Kitties love violence.

230
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,661
[Jimbo meowing]

231
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:51,789
-[grunts]
-If we stop fighting, they'll kill us!

232
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,708
Barely logical and incredibly asinine.
[grunts]

233
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:57,461
Sure sounds like cat to me.

234
00:13:57,545 --> 00:14:01,257
Who cares what they want?
We found you. Let's just escape!

235
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,968
I can't go, not without Gwendolyn!

236
00:14:04,385 --> 00:14:06,804
Dare I inquire who Gwendolyn is?

237
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:12,268
-[meows]
-No. No! You did not get a prison pet!

238
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,769
Jimbo, of all the mistakes!

239
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:18,232
She's not a mistake! She's the one
who saved me when I first got here.

240
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:19,692
She showed me their ways,

241
00:14:19,775 --> 00:14:23,070
got me into the cat-fighting circuit,
made them respect me.

242
00:14:23,153 --> 00:14:24,488
-[meowing]
-[grunting]

243
00:14:25,656 --> 00:14:29,577
We formed the everlasting
and unbreakable bond of baby and pet.

244
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:34,915
-You've been in here, like, ten minutes!
-And they were magical!

245
00:14:35,374 --> 00:14:38,043
-[meows]
-[coughing]

246
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:41,130
-Hairball or the prison pet thing?
-I don't know. Both?

247
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:44,425
-Carry on.
-[coughing]

248
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:46,594
[gasps]

249
00:14:48,929 --> 00:14:50,973
Kelly, is that you? It's Tim.

250
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:54,810
I sat next to you in art.
We shared watercolors. Are you alive?

251
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:58,230
Oh, Tim, you haven't cleaned up
any of this.

252
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:02,318
We really need to get rid of this stuff
if you want that last sticker.

253
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:04,695
This is bigger than stickers, Mom!

254
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:08,782
It looks like Kelly, right?
She's been missing all summer.

255
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:13,454
She went to camp. Can we please
just finish cleaning this dump?

256
00:15:13,537 --> 00:15:17,416
Well, maybe if you worked a little harder,
it wouldn't be such a dump.

257
00:15:17,499 --> 00:15:20,377
I-I didn't mean "dump" dump. [chuckles]

258
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:25,466
Just a friendly reminder.
Keep your eyes on your own work, or else.

259
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:28,177
Or else no sticker for Tim?

260
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:29,970
Sure.

261
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:37,686
Threatening another adult isn't a crime,
Janice. Except it is sort of, Janice.

262
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,856
So, let's please stop talking
to Mommy about robots

263
00:15:40,939 --> 00:15:43,067
and really hustle, baby, okay?

264
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:46,862
Are you really gonna choose
some kitten over us?

265
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:49,698
Uh...

266
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:58,207
I can't choose! I wanna save everybody!
I'm the nice one!

267
00:15:58,290 --> 00:15:59,333
[cats hissing]

268
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,752
[Boss] They're getting restless.
We have to go, Jimbo.

269
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:02,711
[Gwendolyn meows]

270
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:05,381
[growling]

271
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:06,548
[both gasp]

272
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:11,470
[hissing, meowing]

273
00:16:11,553 --> 00:16:13,222
[meowing]

274
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:18,143
-She wants us to follow her. Let's go.
-I don't take orders from a cat.

275
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:19,103
-Whoa!
-Whoa!

276
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,396
[yowling]

277
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:21,855
[snarling]

278
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,402
[grunts]

279
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:32,074
-[meows]
-Ahh! This beast is trying to kill me!

280
00:16:32,157 --> 00:16:35,911
I don't know what's happening,
but I feel so alive!

281
00:16:37,287 --> 00:16:41,000
[sighs] We'll be back home for Dad's
famous pork and beans in no time.

282
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:43,711
-Beans on everything. Yeah!
-[objects clattering]

283
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:46,839
[Jimbo and Staci whimpering]

284
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:49,133
[Boss screams]

285
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:52,970
Danny Petrosky was right. She does
steal kids and turn them into robots!

286
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:57,057
Honey, Danny Petrosky is a liar
and a moron. I'm sorry, but it's true.

287
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:58,642
And now, she's got the baby!

288
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:02,938
What? Tim, what--?
The baby's napping. You're acting crazy.

289
00:17:03,021 --> 00:17:06,608
I've got to stop that evil robot lady.
It's what Dekker Moonboots would do.

290
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,944
Dekker Moonboots would listen
to his mother!

291
00:17:09,028 --> 00:17:11,196
-Don't you dare go in that house!
-Sorry, Mom.

292
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:14,867
Also, if you wanna follow and make sure
everyone's okay and alive, that'd be nice.

293
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,870
[gasps] Timothy Leslie!

294
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:20,414
-[Gwendolyn meows]
-[Boss grunting]

295
00:17:21,999 --> 00:17:23,542
-[Gwendolyn meows]
-[grunts]

296
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:26,211
That's Italian silk, you savage!

297
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,131
Blech!

298
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:31,508
[meows]

299
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:37,097
You made an exit tunnel?
Gwendolyn, you saved everybody!

300
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:42,352
[McCrackin in slow-motion]
Here, kitty, kitty.

301
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,771
-[Gwendolyn meows]
-[Boss grunts]

302
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:47,649
There's a big, fluffy kitty for Mama.

303
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:52,446
Time for you to come upstairs with me now.
Won't that be fun?

304
00:17:52,821 --> 00:17:54,490
Oh, that's a shame.

305
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:57,076
Okay, exit tunnel time!

306
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,412
-Um...
-We can't leave without her!

307
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:04,208
Jimbo, these crazy killer kitties
are gonna find us any second.

308
00:18:04,291 --> 00:18:06,418
We have to get outta here... now!

309
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:10,756
But she just saved our lives.
She saved yours two times.

310
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:15,469
With all due respect, embarrassing,
but he does have a point.

311
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:19,598
Ugh! Sort of. I could've gotten away
on my own. Probably.

312
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:23,018
-So, it's only right that we...
-Send her a proper thank you card?

313
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:26,313
Ugh! Fine. Yes, we'll go save her.

314
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:30,234
-The same way she saved you.
-[chuckles]

315
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:34,738
Saved by a cat. Comedy and danger.
Today's been a real roller coaster.

316
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:39,576
How are we gonna get past all those cats?

317
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:43,413
I have an inside-the-box idea.

318
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:47,626
-[cat meows]
-[cat shrieks]

319
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:53,173
[cats snarling, yowling]

320
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:11,817
[Tim] No. Too late.

321
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:16,572
-Baby... robotomized!
-[Boss] Templeton!

322
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:18,991
You're not a robot!

323
00:19:19,074 --> 00:19:21,243
-What?
-We're looking for Gwendolyn.

324
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,036
-Who?
-[Gwendolyn meows]

325
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:26,206
[licking, coughing]

326
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,833
What?

327
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,218
Do not judge me.

328
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,554
-Mom!
-[Gwendolyn meows]

329
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:43,432
Tim, what--? [gasps]

330
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:45,601
-[cat meowing]
-[device whirring]

331
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,311
[cash register dinging]

332
00:19:47,394 --> 00:19:50,439
-[Mom] Wendi?
-Janice! Uh, I can explain this.

333
00:19:51,231 --> 00:19:52,733
[retching]

334
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:58,280
Those sweaters you gave me...
they're cat hair?

335
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:03,952
I wore them to Thanksgiving, around food!
You said they were cashmere!

336
00:20:04,036 --> 00:20:08,332
I clearly said "cat schmear."
You heard what you wanted.

337
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:12,127
-[police siren wailing]
-Admit it, your wife loved my sweaters!

338
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,086
 Loved the--

339
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:16,924
Turns out Miss McCrackin's
been selling cat hair sweaters

340
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:19,217
at cashmere prices for years.

341
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:21,678
Wow! And we were the ones who busted her?

342
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:24,473
-It was all you, sweetie.
-It's just too bad

343
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:28,101
 that I couldn't actually help her and get
that final Neighborhood Service sticker.

344
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:31,355
You're a Lowly Apprentice Do-Good Trooper?

345
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:36,026
On your way to Lofty Squire
Do-Good Trooper? [chuckles]

346
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:39,196
Well, son, you've done more good
for the neighborhood

347
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:42,241
than any police officer that I ever knew.

348
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:43,659
That's troubling.

349
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:47,371
This is awesome! We did it, Mom!

350
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:51,124
So, lesson learned.
Never judge a book by its cover,

351
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:55,587
even if it turns out the book is even
creepier and weirder on the inside.

352
00:20:55,671 --> 00:20:58,340
Just read a few pages anyway to be sure.

353
00:20:58,423 --> 00:21:00,884
Is any of this helping?
I'm a good mom, right?

354
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:04,096
-I like your head.
-Thanks, kiddo.

355
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:08,141
[police siren wailing]

356
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:11,687
Oh, Gwendolyn, you're the best pet
a baby could have.

357
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:16,984
And we'll be together forever
and ever and ever and ever and ever...

358
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:22,155
-Do you wanna tell him or should I?
-[sighs] Part of being the boss. Jimbo.

359
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:23,573
-...and ev--
-[meows]

360
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:28,787
-[blabbering incoherently]
-You can't have a pet, Jimbo.

361
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:31,540
While this little fur ball
has certainly proven her worth,

362
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:33,041
she's from the other side.

363
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:36,128
You understand? I'm sorry.
It's just the way it is right now.

364
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:37,796
The stakes are too high.

365
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:42,759
That was a very polite way of telling him
that this is gross and unacceptable.

366
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:47,639
[meowing]

367
00:21:50,892 --> 00:21:54,396
Gwendolyn!

368
00:21:59,609 --> 00:22:03,196
-[snarling]
-Darn this mangy kitten! Darn it to heck!

369
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:06,074
Why is it always the last one
that puts up the biggest fight?

370
00:22:06,158 --> 00:22:11,330
-There, there, now.
-Wow! You must have the magic touch.

371
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:14,916
I have always had a special fondness
for kitty cats.

372
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:20,005
You know, looks like you have your van
and your hands mighty full.

373
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:24,051
Would you mind if I took this one?
Seems to have taken a real shine to me.

374
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:29,139
-Uh, strange lanky man, he's all yours.
-[vehicle door closes]

375
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:37,147
Yes, he is. Yes, yes, you are.

376
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:40,275
[cackles]

377
00:22:41,359 --> 00:22:42,486
[theme song playing]

378
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:05,550
♪ Boss Baby ♪

